# Backend connection — one file per connection mode, chosen by the npm script:
#
#   npm run dev          -> .env.ssh     (SSH port forward to the GPU server)
#   npm run dev:pinggy   -> .env.pinggy  (Pinggy tunnel with optional basic auth)
#   npm run dev:local    -> no file      (backend on this machine, http://127.0.0.1:12212)
#
# .env.* files are gitignored — each developer creates their own copies.
# Do not put VITE_API_* in a plain .env: Vite loads it in every mode.
#
# macOS: Finder cannot create dot files. Use Terminal:
#   cd frontend && ./setup-env.sh ssh http://localhost:12212
#   cd frontend && ./setup-env.sh pinggy https://your-tunnel.pinggy.link USER PASSWORD
#
# In dev, Vite proxies /api -> VITE_API_URL and adds auth (avoids browser CORS issues).
#
# --- .env.ssh ---
# Tunnel: ssh -N -L 12212:localhost:12212 -i ~/.ssh/<key> <user>@roihu-gpu.csc.fi
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:12212
#
# --- .env.pinggy ---
# VITE_API_URL=https://your-tunnel.pinggy.link
# VITE_API_USER=your-username
# VITE_API_PASSWORD=your-tunnel-password
